<title>RUSSIA: TABLE - Russia sells 18 trln rbls bills/bonds Aug 6.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Russia sells 18 trln rbls bills/bonds Aug 6.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Finance Ministry will auction 8.00 trillion roubles of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 21083) and 10.00 trillion roubles of 728-day OFZ interest-bearing bonds on August 6, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		    21083</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     8.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Issue date			 Aug 6, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor				364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    Aug 5, 1998</p>
<p>Full details of the bond auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		    24017</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     10.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Issue date			 Aug 6, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor				728 days</p>
<p>    First coupon rate		17.63 pct</p>
<p>    First coupon date		Feb 4, 1998</p>
<p>    Second coupon date	     Aug 5, 1998</p>
<p>    Third coupon date		Feb 3, 1999</p>
<p>    Fourth coupon date	     Aug 4, 1999</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    Aug 4, 1999</p>
<p>In money terms the first coupon amounts to 87,908 roubles.</p>
<p>On August 6, the Finance Ministry will also repay about 6.81 trillion roubles in a maturing 168-day T-bill (series 22073) and pay about 412.6 billion roubles in interest on series 24006 bonds. It will also repay up to 6.42 trillion roubles of the bond early on a voluntary basis.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
